# Affiliate Workflow Tracker

A lightweight static dashboard for managing an affiliate sales pipeline. Drop the three files (`index.html`, `styles.css`, `app.js`) onto any static host (S3, Netlify, Vercel, shared drive, etc.) and you immediately get the UI shown in the screenshot the user provided.

## Features
- Interactable filters for Geo, Model, and Status with one-click reset
- Local data persistence via `localStorage`, so daily updates stay in the same browser
- Modal form for adding or editing deals, plus inline delete actions
- Import ("Import from Gemini") by uploading a JSON file with an array of deal objects
- Export current deals to a timestamped JSON snapshot, or clear everything for a fresh start

## Editing Data Each Day
1. Click `New Deal` to add partners. Use `Edit`/`Delete` icons in the actions column for changes.
2. Filters update automatically as you add new field combinations.
3. All changes store in the browser. Export regularly if you need a backup or want to move data to another machine.

## JSON Shape for Imports
```json
[
  {
    "partner": "Acme Partners",
    "geo": "EMEA",
    "source": "Referral",
    "model": "CPA",
    "status": "Discovery",
    "details": "Any free text",
    "nextSteps": "Next actions",
    "updatedAt": 1732669722000
  }
]
```
Fields other than `partner` are optional. Missing IDs will be created automatically.

## Local Preview
You can open `index.html` directly in your browser, or serve the folder with any static server:

```bash
npx serve .
```

## Deploying
Upload the three files to whatever host you prefer. No build step or backend is required.
